[38;5;252m[1m## What was wrong and what I changed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe bug:[22m In the [38;5;10mcb_luminance[0m function, the Rust translation had incorrect order of operations for the float-to-double promotion compared to the C original.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mC behavior:[22m[0m[0m
[1mc
[0m[38;5;10mpow((R + 0.055) / 1.055, 2.4)
[0m[0m[0m
In C, [38;5;10m0.055[0m is a [38;5;10mdouble[0m literal. When [38;5;10mR[0m (a [38;5;10mfloat[0m) is added to [38;5;10m0.055[0m (a [38;5;10mdouble[0m), C implicitly promotes [38;5;10mR[0m to [38;5;10mdouble[0m [3mbefore[23m the addition. So the entire computation [38;5;10m(R + 0.055) / 1.055[0m happens in [38;5;10mdouble[0m precision.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mRust (buggy) behavior:[22m[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10m((r + 0.055) as f64 / 1.055_f64).powf(2.4) as f32
[0m[0m[0m
Here, [38;5;10mr + 0.055[0m is [38;5;10mf32 + f32[0m (since [38;5;10m0.055[0m is inferred as [38;5;10mf32[0m in an [38;5;10mf32[0m expression context). The addition happens in [38;5;10mf32[0m precision, [3mthen[23m the result is cast to [38;5;10mf64[0m. This loses precision at the addition step.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe fix:[22m Cast [38;5;10mr[0m to [38;5;10mf64[0m [3mbefore[23m adding [38;5;10m0.055[0m, matching C's implicit promotion:[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10m((r as f64 + 0.055) / 1.055_f64).powf(2.4) as f32
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This is a classic C-to-Rust translation pitfall: C's implicit arithmetic promotions (float→double when mixed with double literals) have no equivalent in Rust, where type inference can silently keep everything in [38;5;10mf32[0m.[0m[0m
